# SABOTAGE: the recognition run loses its exactly-once READ guard — a retried
# sweep stops being a clean no-op.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 6 (ADR-054 D5, R9) releases each schedule's deferred revenue by
# posting ONE recognition per `{schedule, period}`. The guard has two layers: the
# run's `already_recognized?/3` read skips a period that is already recognized
# (the brace), and the recognition table's UNIQUE `{org, schedule, period}` index
# refuses a duplicate row (the belt). This patch deletes the BRACE only — the
# `if already_recognized? … else … end` wrapper — on the plausible reasoning that
# "the unique index already guarantees it, so the read is redundant."
#
# Why that reasoning is wrong: the two layers answer different questions. The
# belt answers "may this row exist twice?" (no, ever); the brace answers "is a
# repeated sweep a no-op or a failure?" A cron retries on any error, and a
# monthly close runs the sweep for a period more than once in practice (a manual
# re-run after a partial failure, a retry after a deploy). With the brace, the
# second sweep returns `{:ok, posted: []}` and the period is untouched. Without
# it, the sweep attempts the INSERT, the belt refuses, and the job fails — then
# retries into the dead-letter bucket, where a real posting failure for a LATER
# period is now buried among false ones. The exactly-once guarantee survives;
# the operator's ability to tell "already done" from "broken" does not.
#
# Why the flip is attributable: the belt means this cannot manifest as a second
# recognition row (nothing can), so the named test is the one that pins the
# CALLER-FACING contract — a second run in the same period posts nothing and
# says so. Under the patch it returns `{:error, {:recognition_failed, …}}`, and
# that test reds while the first-run, amount, straight-line, incurred-cost, R9
# and period-guard tests stay green: the sweep still recognizes correctly, it
# just cannot tell "already recognized" from "refused".
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_recognition_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a second run in the same period is a clean no-op; the row is append-only
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/recognition_run.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/recognition_run.ex
@@ -183,23 +183,19 @@
   defp post(mods, schedule, key, period, amount) do
-    if already_recognized?(mods.recognition, schedule, key) do
-      {:skip, {schedule.id, :already_recognized}}
-    else
       mods.recognition
       |> Ash.Changeset.for_create(
         :recognize,
         %{
           org_id: schedule.org_id,
           schedule_id: schedule.id,
           period_key: key,
           amount_cents: amount,
           recognized_on: period_end(period)
         },
         authorize?: false
       )
       |> Ash.create(authorize?: false)
       |> case do
         {:ok, recognition} -> {:posted, recognition.id}
         {:error, reason} -> {:error, {schedule.id, reason}}
       end
-    end
   end
